{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794783475,"nonce":"s2pml4QgAi9TTkXgUGuCEo4WfQE=","title":"Rows lose a stack's upper layer and a nested scroll container's content","message":"When a scroll container is moved by rows, content inside it goes missing:\n\n- an image inside a `stack()` layer above the first (cn avatar with a status dot): the image list is placed as for a plain image (same row, clip, clip_from), yet it does not show; the dot does.\n- a scroll container nested in the moved one (cn scroll area demos): its content is lost on some frames (289 px against the full paint in the harness scene).\n\nPresent at b775d936, before the clip-path rows change; it showed in cn_demo once the page itself qualified for rows. Harness scene 'scroll a page with clips of its own' in blinc_recorder animation_paths reproduces both (VARIANT=stack / VARIANT=scroll env in a local copy split them; not committed).\n\nGuarded for now: `scroll_node_qualifies` keeps a container with a stack layer or a nested scroll container off rows, so cn_demo's page scroll is full paints again (census: nested scroll 7, stack layer 8). Remove the guard when fixed and put the scene in ON_ROWS.","files":null}]}